Ladybird now accepts an escaped ClassSetReservedPunctuator and a
control escape in a v-mode class and in \q{}, and parses \q{} escapes
with the same grammar as a class set operand. V8 does the same: In its
kInClass state, ParseCharacterEscape() accepts every character that
IsClassSetReservedPunctuator() matches. And its parser reads \q{} with
ParseClassStringDisjunction(), which takes each character through
ParseClassSetCharacter(). Gecko imports that parser as is, in
js/src/irregexp/imported/regexp-parser.cc. And in WebKit, YarrParser’s
isIdentityEscapeAnError() accepts the same punctuators in both its
ClassSet and its ClassStringDisjunction escape modes.
